    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math intuitive, especially through chemistry and computer science. As a retired teacher, I see patterns in nature and data, which makes math feel like a language rather than a chore. My hobbies like photography and board games also help me visualize concepts, so I approach it with curiosity and practicality.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. My neuroticism score is low, and I’ve learned to reframe math as a problem-solving tool. When I’m stuck, I take breaks for yoga or birdwatching—activities that calm my mind and help me return to the problem with clarity.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used AI tools like Wolfram Alpha for quick checks on equations and to visualize graphs. It helped me verify my work without frustration. I didn’t rely on it for deep learning but found it useful for small, practical tasks.",
